{
  "pages": [
    {
      "page_idx": 22,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "header",
          "bbox": [
            0.689,
            0.048,
            0.86,
            0.066
          ],
          "content": "Fractions in Disguise"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.089,
            0.848,
            0.148
          ],
          "content": "2. Bank of Wahapur offers an interest of 5% p.a. Compare how much one gets if one deposits ₹20,000 for a period of 4 years with compounding and without compounding annually."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.156,
            0.846,
            0.194
          ],
          "content": "3. Do you observe anything interesting in the solutions of the two questions above? Share and discuss."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.198,
            0.801,
            0.22
          ],
          "content": "Let us try to generalise the pattern observed in each of the options."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.112,
            0.227,
            0.845,
            0.268
          ],
          "content": "？ **Example 9:** What is the amount we get back if we invest ₹6000 at an interest rate of 10% p.a. for ‘t’ years?"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.276,
            0.342,
            0.297
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "No Compounding"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.3,
            0.848,
            0.357
          ],
          "content": "Here, the interest gained every term is paid back. Therefore, the principal amount for every term shall remain the same, and as a result, the interest gained every term also shall be the same."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.37,
            0.485,
            0.405
          ],
          "content": "The interest gained in 1 term is 6000 × 0.1 The interest gained in 3 terms is"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.239,
            0.404,
            0.364,
            0.421
          ],
          "content": "6 0 0 0 \\times 0 . 1 \\times 3",
          "image_source": "images/page_22_equation_8.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.117,
            0.421,
            0.484,
            0.454
          ],
          "content": "The total amount at the end of an FD of 3 years is"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.199,
            0.454,
            0.401,
            0.473
          ],
          "content": "6 0 0 0 \\div ( 6 0 0 0 \\times 0 . 1 \\times 3 ) .",
          "image_source": "images/page_22_equation_10.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.494,
            0.37,
            0.883,
            0.422
          ],
          "content": "The interest gained in 1 term is p × r (p is the principal, r is the rate of interest in percentage)"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.544,
            0.421,
            0.832,
            0.44
          ],
          "content": "The interest gained in t terms is"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.65,
            0.439,
            0.729,
            0.455
          ],
          "content": "p \\times r \\times t",
          "image_source": "images/page_22_equation_13.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.506,
            0.454,
            0.871,
            0.487
          ],
          "content": "The total amount at the end of an FD of t years is"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.587,
            0.488,
            0.787,
            0.524
          ],
          "content": "p + (p \\times r \\times t) = p + rrt",
          "image_source": "images/page_22_equation_15.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.555,
            0.364,
            0.575
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "With Compounding"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.578,
            0.847,
            0.637
          ],
          "content": "Here, the interest gained every term/year is added back to the FD. Therefore, the principal amount increases after every term, and as a result, the interest gained every term also increases proportionately."
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "bbox": [
            0.118,
            0.65,
            0.494,
            0.873
          ],
          "sub_type": "algorithm",
          "content": "The total amount in the FD after Year 1 is\n$\\widehat{(6000) \\times 1.1}$\n(principal for Year 1)\nThe total amount in the FD after Year 2 is\n$\\hat{(6000 \\times 1.1) \\times 1.1}$\n(principal for Year 2)\nThe total amount in the FD after Year 3 is\n$\\angle (6000 \\times 1.1 \\times 1.1) \\times 1.1$\n(principal for Year 3)\nThe total amount in the FD after t years is\n6000 × (1.1 × 1.1 × 1.1…..× 1.1)\nt times\n6000 × (1.1)t.",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.507,
            0.65,
            0.877,
            0.67
          ],
          "content": "The total amount in the FD after Year 1 is"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.558,
            0.668,
            0.743,
            0.686
          ],
          "content": "\\frac{(p) \\times (1 + r)}{}",
          "image_source": "images/page_22_equation_20.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.505,
            0.685,
            0.695,
            0.703
          ],
          "content": "(principal for Year 1)"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.506,
            0.701,
            0.876,
            0.719
          ],
          "content": "The total amount in the FD after Year 2 is"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.549,
            0.719,
            0.772,
            0.736
          ],
          "content": "p \\times (1 + r) \\times (1 + r)",
          "image_source": "images/page_22_equation_23.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.505,
            0.735,
            0.695,
            0.753
          ],
          "content": "(principal for Year 2)"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.506,
            0.752,
            0.877,
            0.77
          ],
          "content": "The total amount in the FD after Year 3 is"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.546,
            0.77,
            0.807,
            0.787
          ],
          "content": "\\curvearrowleft p \\times ( 1 + r ) \\times ( 1 + r ) \\times ( 1 + r )",
          "image_source": "images/page_22_equation_26.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.505,
            0.786,
            0.695,
            0.804
          ],
          "content": "(principal for Year 3)"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.505,
            0.803,
            0.88,
            0.821
          ],
          "content": "The total amount in the FD after t years is"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.552,
            0.82,
            0.829,
            0.872
          ],
          "content": "\\begin{array}{c}\\mathrm{p} \\times(1+r) \\times(1+r) \\times \\cdots \\times(1+r) \\\\t \\operatorname{timeses} \\\\\\mathrm{p} \\times(1+\\mathrm{r})^{\\mathrm{t}} .\\end{array}",
          "image_source": "images/page_22_equation_29.jpg"
        },
